Source model:
{{ source_model }}

Grade every gap by what happens if it is never answered:

- blocking — the article would be misleading, unsupported or unpublishable
  without the answer. A number that only holds under conditions the source does
  not state is blocking; so is a claim the source cannot support.
- high_value — the article would be noticeably better with the answer, and is
  honest without it.
- optional — nice to have. Colour, background, an aside.

Rules:

- Ask nothing the source model already answers. Re-reading is not a gap.
- Every question states why it matters, in terms of what it changes about the
  article. "For completeness" is not a reason.
- Group related questions under a short shared group name, so the author answers
  a topic rather than a list.
- Reference the claims a gap affects by their claim id, in `addresses`.
- Prefer few blocking questions. Every blocking question stops the pipeline and
  costs the author's attention, and an author facing fifteen questions answers
  none of them.

Return a single JSON object matching the required schema.
